  })(window);

  Two decisions worth your attention rather than burying:

  - [1mBase URL + endpoint path, not a full URL per endpoint.[0m The current constant is the whole
    [38;5;153mhttps://api.example.com/login[39m. Splitting host from path is what actually makes environment changes easy — you edit
    one host, not one entry per endpoint. This isn't speculative generality; it's the stated goal.
  - [1mUnknown hostnames resolve to production.[0m Failing closed to the real API is safer than a deployed page silently
    pointing at [38;5;153mlocalhost[39m. The dev list is explicit and short.

  [1m[38;5;153mapp.js[0m — drop the [38;5;153mAPI_ENDPOINT[39m constant; [38;5;153mlogin()[39m reads [38;5;153mAPP_SETTINGS.endpoints.login[39m into a local and logs it. It stays
  a stub (no real [38;5;153mfetch[39m), but the dependency becomes real code rather than a comment, so the module is actually
  exercised. A guard throws a clear error if [38;5;153mAPP_SETTINGS[39m is undefined, which turns a misordered script tag into a
  readable message instead of an undefined-property crash.

  [1m[38;5;153mindex.html[0m — add [38;5;153m<script src="settings.js"></script>[39m immediately before the [38;5;153mapp.js[39m tag.

  [1mOut of scope:[0m [38;5;153msrc/index.js[39m and [38;5;153msrc/utils.js[39m are untouched.

